  "pixel_findings": [
    "Tower dormer cap ends: clock_tower and pavilion_mansard show continuous pale closure at the previously open cap/cheek corners; earlier sharp black notches are absent. Roof_court confirms both visible tower faces. Original broad tympanum openings remain closed.",
    "Porch staircase: porch_stair and side elevations retain solid stair cheeks and continuous contact with the ground and upper landing. No floating stair assembly is visible.",
    "Envelope and openings: all four exterior elevations retain consistent framed recessed glazing and supported trim; glass_close shows room depth through the panes. Interior supplies a window-facing occupied-space proof, though not whole-building circulation verification.",
    "Roof and courtyard: aerial, top, roof_court and rear_court show a continuous perimeter roof, four supported corner pavilions, central clock tower and open courtyard with finished walls and windows. No new silhouette, disconnected roof contact or courtyard regression is visible.",
    "Identity and composition: central civic clock tower, stepped mansards, corner pavilions, two principal facade levels above a basement, columned porch and entry stair remain legible against all three locked sources."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Architectural-clay pass only. Source segmental clock-face pediments are simplified to triangular pediments; tower crown and lantern, roof seams, masonry ornament and ironwork are abstracted.",
    "Ordinary source dormer glazing is largely rectangular beneath a segmental hood; the model uses arched apertures. This remains a documented source-detail simplification at this gate.",
    "The first phone board compares different camera scale and angle; direct source images and all full-size render files were inspected independently of the board.",
    "No browser material, placement, save/reload, walkability, terrain fit, scaling, performance or human keeper approval is claimed."
  ],
